// REJECTS: no viable alternative at input '[{'
//
// A GenerationSpecification written in the ###FileGeneration section. The two generation
// sections are adjacent, similarly named, and route to different grammars.
//
// What makes this worth a fixture is that it does not fail where you would expect. The
// element keyword is NOT checked: `fileGeneration: identifier qualifiedName { ... }` accepts
// `GenerationSpecification` as a generation type quite happily. It fails only further in,
// when `generationNodes: [ { ... } ]` turns out not to be a legal config property value. A
// rewrite that validates the section's element keyword instead would reject this too --
// for a reason legend-engine does not have.
###FileGeneration
GenerationSpecification fixture::neg::SpecInWrongSection
{
   generationNodes: [
      {
         generationElement: fixture::neg::AvroConfig;
      }
   ];
}
